  "id": "cses",
  "term": "CSES",
  "definition": "CSEs are crime scene examiners, professionals who gather and interpret physical evidence to help reconstruct what happened at a crime scene. In psychology-related discussions, their role is notable because it involves sustained sensory, cognitive, and organizational stress while working closely with graphic or traumatic material.",
